adaptations to every vendored source file:

1. Relative TypeScript import/export suffixes changed from `.ts` to `.js` so
   this repository's NodeNext compilation resolves emitted JavaScript.
2. A leading `// @ts-nocheck` notice was added because Faultline enables
   `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`; the pinned upstream project does not. Its own
   strict TypeScript configuration succeeds without that additional option.

No runtime engine behavior was changed. The focused adapter test removes the
leading notice, reverses the import suffix change, and checks each resulting
source file against its pinned upstream SHA-256 digest.
